# Optional browser runtime

<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-v1-guides.ts from executed canonical source. Do not edit this output by hand. -->

V2-02 adds the first optional browser-only entrypoint. It is a loading and
private transport boundary, not enhanced navigation yet. Native links and forms
remain the complete behavior, and importing the browser facade alone performs
no startup work.

The application build owns a generated entry that imports only the public
browser facade and starts it explicitly:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/browser-entry.ts","language":"ts"} -->

The current packed-package gate renders that entry through the real renderer,
links it to browser files from the same installed tarball, and runs it in all
three supported browser engines. The normalized successful observation is:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/success.json","language":"json"} -->

Startup outside a browser document is a stable refusal and does not expose a
second runtime mode:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/refusal.json","language":"json"} -->

The flow record makes the current ownership and deliberately skipped work
explicit:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/flow.json","language":"json"} -->

Wrong or missing nonce, a missing module, disabled JavaScript, and operational
rollback all leave the native page usable. Rollback stops module emission and
restores the renderer's `script-src 'none'` policy:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/recovery.json","language":"json"} -->

Run `pnpm check:v2-browser-runtime` for the clean packed consumer and 18
three-engine cases. Run `pnpm check:v2-patch-protocol` for exact envelope,
malformed input, raw byte, structural depth/count, duration, cancellation,
cross-generation isolation, and redaction evidence. The update protocol remains
private, and no analyzer/editor schema is added.
